WEBVTT

00:00:09,360 --> 00:00:13,140
How often should I run standard labs?

00:00:13,140 --> 00:00:17,420
Well, that's another, it depends answer to this.

00:00:17,420 --> 00:00:22,420
So it depends on if your standard labs

00:00:22,860 --> 00:00:24,980
have been running normal

00:00:25,980 --> 00:00:27,920
and you're not doing anything different

00:00:27,920 --> 00:00:32,920
as things that would cause abnormalities.

00:00:34,620 --> 00:00:37,300
Let's say you're not taking medication,

00:00:37,300 --> 00:00:40,220
that could cause issues with your liver markers,

00:00:40,220 --> 00:00:41,780
you're not taking fed medicine,

00:00:41,780 --> 00:00:44,220
that could cause issues with your liver markers,

00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:45,620
then you can spread those out.

00:00:45,620 --> 00:00:46,860
So it's all depends on,

00:00:46,860 --> 00:00:48,780
hey, my last labs were normal.

00:00:48,780 --> 00:00:51,580
Well, when were the ones before that?

00:00:51,580 --> 00:00:52,980
Two months were those normal?

00:00:52,980 --> 00:00:54,060
Those were a little bit off.

00:00:54,060 --> 00:00:57,060
Okay, let's maybe go three months on these.

00:00:57,060 --> 00:00:59,260
Or my last labs were abnormal.

00:00:59,260 --> 00:01:01,500
You had me run them again this month.

00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:03,300
And now they're still abnormal.

00:01:03,300 --> 00:01:06,060
We're gonna still keep running them on a monthly basis.

00:01:06,060 --> 00:01:08,500
So it depends on what we're looking at,

00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:09,980
what we're dealing with.

00:01:09,980 --> 00:01:13,300
But in general, how often should anybody run labs

00:01:13,300 --> 00:01:17,260
if they were consistently normal?

00:01:17,260 --> 00:01:20,100
Well, if you have a major change of symptoms,

00:01:20,100 --> 00:01:23,820
you should investigate why you have that change of symptoms.

00:01:23,820 --> 00:01:25,700
But otherwise, I don't think it's wrong

00:01:25,700 --> 00:01:30,220
for a healthy person with no diagnosis to wait a year

00:01:30,220 --> 00:01:33,500
to run labs to make sure everything is normal.

00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:34,340
That makes sense.

00:01:34,340 --> 00:01:37,380
You're just trying to use some reasonableness

00:01:37,380 --> 00:01:39,900
in your investigations.

